  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A Streamlit app that computes theoretical c/z or b/y fragment ions for a demo or pasted protein sequence, matches them against a synthetic, bundled-mzML, uploaded-mzML or pasted MS2 peak list within a ppm tolerance, and reports coverage, a mirror plot and a per-ion mass-error table you can export. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
